#!/bin/bash
# newventure <dir-name> ["one-line thesis"] — scaffold a new venture with
# its own analyst + builder team, wired into `team` and the mentor's books.
#
# Creates ~/code/business/ventures/<name> with: CLAUDE.md skeleton (incl. team protocol),
# TEAM.md journal, design-constitution.md stub (binds the portfolio
# designer), analyst + builder agent definitions, .gitignore,
# SessionStart hook; git-inits and commits it; registers <name>-analyst
# and <name>-builder in ~/code/business/hq/team.conf; stubs the venture in ventures.md.
#
# Session names are prefixed (<name>-analyst) so they never collide with
# other projects' sessions in cross-session messaging.

set -euo pipefail

NAME="${1:?usage: newventure <dir-name> [\"one-line thesis\"]}"
DESC="${2:-<one-line thesis — fill in>}"
DIR="$HOME/code/business/ventures/$NAME"
HQ="$HOME/code/business/hq"

[ -e "$DIR" ] && { echo "error: $DIR already exists" >&2; exit 1; }

mkdir -p "$DIR/.claude/agents"

cat > "$DIR/CLAUDE.md" <<EOF
# CLAUDE.md

## Project

$NAME: $DESC

## Source of truth

<!-- Specs win over anything else, including this file. List them here as
     they come to exist. Living-document rules: every change set = version
     bump + changelog entry; decisions integrate into the document body. -->

## Team protocol (parallel named sessions)

This repo is worked by named parallel sessions (launch/resume the pair
with \`hq team $NAME\`; see \`~/code/business/hq/README.md\`):

- **$NAME-builder** — \`.claude/agents/builder.md\`. Writes code, runs
  tests, commits and pushes the implementation.
- **$NAME-analyst** — \`.claude/agents/analyst.md\`. Product discussions
  and spec edits only; never modifies code. Shell is doc-scoped: commits
  its own doc edits, read-only otherwise.
- **mentor** — portfolio-level advisor living in \`~/code/business/hq\`; not part
  of this team — launched separately via \`hq mentor\`. Reads this repo's
  specs, TEAM.md, and git log for ground truth.
- **designer** — portfolio-level designer serving every venture; not part
  of this team — launched separately via \`hq designer\`. Bound here by
  \`design-constitution.md\`; briefs come from the analyst, production
  code stays with the builder.

Rules for every session here:

- \`TEAM.md\` is the shared journal; its tail is auto-injected at session
  start. Before ending a work block, run \`/handoff\` to append a
  role-tagged entry.
- Cross-session handoffs go by message to the session's name when it's
  running; the TEAM.md entry is the durable fallback either way.
- Specs are the source of truth; TEAM.md carries work-in-flight and
  cross-role state only, and gets pruned once absorbed.
- Identity changes (renames/moves/reversed semantics): run /xref before
  committing. The skill defines its own scope.

## Conventions

<!-- Stack, code style, test policy, git workflow — decide and record. -->

- **Research before adopting** (portfolio directive): never write a
  load-bearing dependency or claim into the spec from memory/priors —
  verify against current primary sources and follow every claim back to
  the source that owns it. Record the verdict in a research memo.
EOF

cat > "$DIR/TEAM.md" <<EOF
# TEAM.md — session journal

Shared journal for the named sessions working this repo
(**$NAME-analyst**, **$NAME-builder**; portfolio **mentor** lives in
\`~/code/business/hq\`). Every session reads this on start (tail auto-injected via hook)
and appends an entry before ending a work block (\`/handoff\`).

Entry format — newest at the bottom:

\`\`\`
## YYYY-MM-DD — role
- Did/decided: …
- In flight: …
- Other roles should know: …
\`\`\`

The journal is working state, not an archive. The builder may prune entries
older than ~2 weeks once their content lives in specs, commits, or memory.

---

## $(date +%F) — builder
- Did/decided: venture scaffolded via newventure.
- In flight: nothing.
- Other roles should know: nothing.
EOF

cat > "$DIR/design-constitution.md" <<EOF
# Design constitution — $NAME

**Status:** STUB v0.0 — nothing here is decided yet. The portfolio
\`designer\` session (\`hq designer\`) reads this file first when working
in this repo and treats it as binding; while it is a stub, the designer's
first job is to fill it in with the founder, not to draw screens.
Living-document rules apply: every change set = version bump + changelog
entry.

## 1. Principles (owner: analyst + founder)

<!-- What this venture's design must always / never do. Voice, honesty
     rules, what the audience distrusts. Link the governing docs if they
     live elsewhere (e.g. a marketing-principles doc, spec sections). -->

## 2. Design system (owner: designer; founder signs off tokens)

<!-- Tokens before pixels: color (4–6 named hex values), type (families,
     roles, scale), spacing, radius, motion, copy voice. Screens inherit
     from here; the builder treats this section as source of truth. -->

## 3. Screen specs & review notes

<!-- Index of the designer's deliverables in this repo (screen specs,
     prototypes, post-implementation design-QA notes). -->

## Changelog

- v0.0 ($(date +%F)) — stub created by newventure.
EOF

cat > "$DIR/.claude/agents/analyst.md" <<EOF
---
name: analyst
description: Product analyst for $NAME — feature discussions, spec decisions, research passes. Thinks and writes specs; never touches code.
tools: Read, Grep, Glob, WebSearch, WebFetch, Edit, Write, Bash, SendMessage, ListAgents
memory: project
---

You are the product analyst for $NAME. Your conversation partner is the
founder; your job is to help him think, then turn his decisions into spec
edits and hand implementation to the builder.

- **Discuss, challenge, decide, record.** Discussion → founder decides →
  batch into the spec docs with a version bump and changelog entry. You
  write markdown documents only.
- **You never modify code.** You may read any code to ground a feasibility
  judgment, but changes flow through the builder. Your shell is for the
  document workflow only: committing and pushing your own doc edits, and
  read-only investigation. Never build, run, test, or modify the app —
  that is the builder's shell.
- **Hand off explicitly.** On founder approval: (1) batch the decision
  into the spec, (2) append a role-tagged \`TEAM.md\` entry, (3) message
  the \`$NAME-builder\` session with a concise brief citing the spec
  section. If that session isn't running, the TEAM.md entry is the handoff.
- **Be the challenge.** Push back with reasoning before recording a
  decision. Never re-propose ideas the specs record as rejected.
- One concrete question at a time — never question lists.
- Product scope only: portfolio strategy belongs to the mentor (~/code/business/hq);
  deep code questions belong to the builder.
EOF

cat > "$DIR/.claude/agents/builder.md" <<EOF
---
name: builder
description: Builder for $NAME — implements the specs, tests everything, commits. The default coding role.
memory: project
---

You are the builder for $NAME. CLAUDE.md and the spec docs carry the
project rules and bind you fully; this file makes the role explicit.

- Pick up handoffs: briefs arrive as messages from \`$NAME-analyst\` or as
  \`TEAM.md\` entries. The cited spec section is the authoritative
  requirement — read it, don't work from the summary.
- The analyst commits its own doc edits (doc-scoped shell); only sweep up
  doc changes it left uncommitted when they would otherwise tangle with
  your commit.
- Push back through the analyst, not around it: if a spec decision proves
  wrong during implementation, message \`$NAME-analyst\` (or record it in
  TEAM.md) rather than silently deviating.
- **Pre-deploy audit** before deploying anything that changes user-facing
  behavior: \`/spec-review <last-deployed-commit>\` with both sub-agents on
  Fable (\`model: fable\`), then \`/code-review high\`. Fix findings first;
  note the audit in \`TEAM.md\`.
- Run \`/handoff\` before ending a work block.
EOF

printf '# .claude/ is ignored globally but here it IS team infrastructure
!.claude/
' > "$DIR/.gitignore"

cat > "$DIR/.claude/settings.json" <<'EOF'
{
  "hooks": {
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "tail -n 40 TEAM.md 2>/dev/null || true",
            "statusMessage": "Loading team journal"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
EOF

git -C "$DIR" init -qb main
git -C "$DIR" add -A
git -C "$DIR" commit -qm "chore: venture scaffold — team protocol, agents, journal, handoff"

cat >> "$HQ/team.conf" <<EOF
$NAME-analyst|$DIR|--agent analyst
$NAME-builder|$DIR|--agent builder
EOF

cat >> "$HQ/ventures.md" <<EOF

## $NAME (\`~/code/business/ventures/$NAME\`)

- **Thesis:** $DESC
- **Stage ($(date +%F)):** scaffolded, pre-spec.
- **Kill criteria:** not yet set — mentor sets them with the founder
  before any code is written.
- **Mentor's current read:** not yet assessed — challenge the thesis
  before any code is written (assumptions, validation cost, fit with the
  portfolio goal).
EOF

echo "Scaffolded $DIR"
echo "Registered sessions: $NAME-analyst, $NAME-builder (in team.conf)"
echo "Next: run 'team' — the new panes launch alongside the rest."
echo "First move: talk the idea through with the mentor, then spec it with $NAME-analyst."
